course: dictionary
lesson: 16066
title: Voluble: talking a lot
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Voluble is a describing word for someone who talks a lot, quickly and easily, often with feeling. «Our voluble guide told us about every bird in the park before we had even reached the gate.» The guide did not stop talking, so voluble means talking a great deal.
explain: The word can also describe speech. «Her voluble speech about recycling went on for ten minutes, with word after word.» Here it means long, fast and full of words. Test your meaning by swapping in talkative. If the sentence still makes sense, you are on the right track.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Phrases like «never stops» or «could not get a word in» tell you someone is voluble. Toad in The Wind in the Willows is voluble: he never stops talking about himself.
fact: Voluble means talking a lot, quickly and easily, often with feeling.
fact: «Voluble» can also describe speech that is long, fast and full of words.
fact: «Voluble» is a formal word, so you will meet it more often in books than in everyday talk.
fact: Talkative is a close synonym, but voluble suggests talking more smoothly and with more feeling.
fact: The opposite of voluble is quiet, or silent.
exercise: «Toad was so voluble about his new car that nobody else could get a word in.» What does voluble mean here? | Sleepy after a long lunch | *Talking a lot and fast | Angry and shouting | Very quiet and still
exercise: Ella says voluble means quiet. Why is she wrong? | *It means talking a lot, not being quiet | It means small | It means lost | It means quiet
exercise: «The shy boy gave only short answers, so he was not voluble at all.» What does this sentence suggest? | He could not speak | *He talked very little | He sang every word | He talked for hours
test: Which word is closest in meaning to voluble? | *Talkative | Sleepy | Shy | Silent
test: Which sentence uses voluble correctly? | *The voluble man talked about his holiday for an hour without stopping. | The voluble door was closed. | Voluble he ate his soup quietly. | The voluble cup was full of tea.
exam: In Alice in Wonderland, the Mock Turtle is voluble. What does this tell the reader about him? | *He talks a great deal | He cannot see well | He is very tiny | He sleeps all day
